{
  "_comment": "sc-18810 two-dimensional geometry sweep for mlx:ltx_2_3. Standalone, like the sc-18808 plan:\na video row in config/memory-calibration-plan.json still matches no matrix coordinate (sc-18817\nfolds these in).\n\nDESIGN. Two spatial-latent levels (768x512 and 512x768 are 24x16 = 384 latent cells; 1280x704 and\n704x1280 are 40x22 = 880) crossed with three frame levels each. Crossing two AREAS is what makes the\ncandidates separable at all: with one area the `mpx` column is proportional to the intercept, so BOTH\nthe additive `perFrame` and the `perMpxFrame` cross designs are singular and neither coefficient is\nidentifiable (pinned by scripts/fit-ltx-temporal-form.test.mjs). fps is held at 30 except for one\ndeliberate probe.\n\nRUNGS ARE NOT UNIFORM ACROSS THE ENVELOPE. The LTX VAE decode auto-selects tiling and the bound that\nbinds first is machine-INDEPENDENT: `VaeTiling::LTX.writable_frame_cap(h, w) = i32::MAX / (8*h*w)`\n(gen-core/src/tiling.rs:166, full_res_channels 8) is 682 / 682 / 655 / 297 / 297 over the five\ndeclared resolutions, so only the two 0.90 MP buckets reach it inside the 449-frame envelope, at 298\noutput frames. `fit` and `held_out` points are therefore all rung-1 single-pass decodes; the\n`rung2_boundary` points are rung 2. Fitting one curve across that break would fit through a\ncapability change.\n\nMEMORY IS NON-MONOTONIC IN FRAMES, which is why the frame levels stop where they do. The engine's own\nsingle-pass decode model is `3.3 GB + 340 B/output voxel`, so at 1280x704 the decode cost climbs to\n~94 GB at f297 -- the write cap -- and then COLLAPSES to ~19 GB at f305 once tiling engages\n(`3.3 GB + 40 B/voxel + 300 B/tile-voxel`). The most expensive geometry in the declared envelope is\nthe cap, not the maximum.\n\n`not_attempted_host_limit` records that honestly. On this host (128 GiB unified, and free disk is\nwhat bounds swap) a single-pass decode near the cap drives MLX's elastic allocator cache past\nphysical memory: 704x1280 x 177 (159,498,240 voxels) completed with 54.15 GB active + 90.68 GiB\ncache = 114.98 GiB CO-EXISTING, and 768x512 x 449 (176,553,984 voxels) was killed by a signal with\nfree disk falling 81 -> 16 GiB. The three `not_attempted_host_limit` geometries all sit above that\nline (176.6M / 217.2M / 267.6M voxels) and were not attempted rather than burned. This is a HOST\nverdict, not a model verdict, and it was reached before any curve was fitted -- role assignment here\nis a feasibility decision and never referenced a residual.\n\nROLES. `fit` trains the candidates. `held_out` is never fitted: a third area (640x640, 400 latent\ncells) and both transposed aspect ratios. `held_out_fps_probe` re-renders an identical\n{w,h,frames} at 24 fps to measure the audio-latent axis GeometryEnvelope cannot express.\n`reproduction_probe` re-renders the geometry behind sc-18809's WITHDRAWN 43.87 GiB figure (bf16,\n768x512 x 145 = the declared 6 s x 24 fps cell) on the production full-A/V path, so the two compare\nonly as an inequality. `rung2_boundary` covers f305 (one lattice step past the cap) and the envelope\nmaximum f449.\n\nDrive with: node scripts/memory-calibration-harness.mjs run --config\ndocs/calibration/sc-18810/ltx-mlx-geometry-sweep.json --backend mlx --provider <name>\n--fresh-per-case --provider-command '[\"<target>/release/memory-mlx-adapter\"]' --sceneworks-repo\n<repo> --inference-repo <inference-at-pin> --resume <out.json> --output <out.json>, with --output\nOUTSIDE the repo and SCENEWORKS_LTX_{REPOSITORY,REVISION,ROOT,TEXT_ENCODER_ROOT} set.",
